// Real-agent BasicSummon (the `find_familiar.ron` shape): a fighting/bearing
// companion, not a decorative phantasm -- matches "forging a lasting bond...
// ready to serve and bear you into battle."
// `alignment`/`with_agent`/`incorporeal`/`phantom_illusion` all left at their
// `#[serde(default)]` values (owned, agentic, solid, real), and
// `duration: None` for a permanent bond (recast doesn't despawn/replace a
// prior steed -- no cap exists on this summon path, same as
// `find_familiar.ron`). `body: QuadrupedMedium(Horse)` stands in for "a swift
// and intelligent mount" -- no in-cast mount-selection UI exists, so one
// representative mount body is picked rather than exposing a choice the
// engine can't offer yet.
//
// Same known gap as `find_familiar.ron`, not re-derived here: `BasicSummon`'s
// `CreateNpcEvent` path never populates `comp::Pet`, so this steed will NOT
// survive a logout/server-restart and isn't chunk-unload-protected. See
// `find_familiar.ron`'s own comment for the mechanism.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 3.0),
        body: QuadrupedMedium((species: Horse, body_type: Female)),
        scale: None,
        has_health: true,
        use_npc_name: true,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: None,
    ),
)
